  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> according to the following equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;molecule is paramagnetic, as it contains odd number of electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>ClO<sub>2</sub> is used as a bleaching agent for paper pulp and textiles and in water treatment</p></blockquote>"
